Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.87,0:00:12.24,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Look at all these people, Kate.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.73,0:00:14.75,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Do you think there's a festival?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.14,0:00:17.61,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Come on, Connie. Let's go home.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.90,0:00:18.74,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,But—
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.82,0:00:23.87,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Kate?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.64,0:00:28.75,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Kate! Where are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.28,0:01:13.73,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Wow...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.61,0:01:16.25,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,She's so pretty.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.28,0:01:23.80,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,A curse on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.51,0:01:28.13,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,A curse upon you all!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.07,0:01:36.49,Default,Man,0,0,0,,Y-You fiend!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.32,0:01:38.48,Default,Crowd,0,0,0,,Fiend!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.48,0:01:39.69,Default,Crowd,0,0,0,,Murderess!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.69,0:01:40.76,Default,Crowd,0,0,0,,Hear, hear!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.76,0:01:42.83,Default,Crowd,0,0,0,,You're the cursed one!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.05,0:02:35.25,Default,Crowd,0,0,0,,It's over! She's dead!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.25,0:02:36.43,Default,Crowd,0,0,0,,Dead and gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.43,0:02:37.75,Default,Crowd,0,0,0,,Serves her right!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.69,0:02:57.15,Signs,Signs,0,0,0,,LESSER PALACE (GRAND MERILLIAN)
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.45,0:03:03.86,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,{\an8}It's been ten years since that night \Nin Saint Mark's Square,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.38,0:03:08.14,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,{\an8}and I, Constance Grail, am now sixteen.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.03,0:03:14.54,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,{\an8}Allow me to congratulate you, Miss Grail.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.54,0:03:18.55,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Thank you very much, Viscount Hamsworth.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.55,0:03:22.91,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Surely the Fates will bless your union,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.91,0:03:27.87,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,what with the Grail family motto \Nof "Be you sincere."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.32,0:03:32.55,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,"Be you sincere," huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.31,0:03:35.65,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,This all started a few months ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.65,0:03:39.06,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,My father, the living embodiment \Nof the Grail family's sincerity,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.39,0:03:42.07,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,found himself under a mountain of debt.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.16,0:03:45.53,Flashback,Ethel,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Connie.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.44,0:03:48.98,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,On the condition that \Nthe Bronson Company pay it,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.98,0:03:54.05,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I became engaged to \NMr. Bronson's son and heir, Neil.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.62,0:03:57.95,Flashback,Neil,0,0,0,,Neil Bronson, at your service.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.66,0:04:03.15,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I can't deny that I'd dreamed\N of marrying for love.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.00,0:04:07.98,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,But a plain, dull girl like me,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.98,0:04:12.28,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,getting a handsome, well-mannered gentleman\N to consent to become her husband?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.28,0:04:13.94,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I should consider myself blessed...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.38,0:04:15.99,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Or so I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.02,0:04:18.99,Flashback,Mylene,0,0,0,,I heard the news, Connie!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.26,0:04:22.03,Flashback,Mylene,0,0,0,,You're engaged to Neil Bronson,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.03,0:04:25.74,Flashback,Mylene,0,0,0,,but everyone is talking \Nabout him and Pamela Francis!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.02,0:04:27.87,Flashback,Connie,0,0,0,,Pamela Francis?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.87,0:04:32.88,Flashback,Mylene,0,0,0,,Yes! Someone saw them in each other's arms \Nwhen they thought no one was watching!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.88,0:04:38.37,Flashback,Mylene,0,0,0,,It seems Neil simply worships her. \NDon't you think, Kate?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.37,0:04:42.75,Flashback,Kate,0,0,0,,Really, Mylene, you should stop \Nspreading groundless rumors.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.20,0:04:47.39,Flashback,Kate,0,0,0,,No one would act that way after \Njust getting engaged, and you know it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.39,0:04:49.38,Flashback,Mylene,0,0,0,,I wouldn't be so sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.38,0:04:54.66,Flashback,Mylene,0,0,0,,I hear Pamela goes through men the way\Nthe rest of us go through dance partners.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.66,0:04:58.40,Flashback,Kate,0,0,0,,Really, there is such a thing \Nas delicacy, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.92,0:05:04.15,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I trust Neil.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.62,0:05:07.39,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,He was his usual kind self \Nto me this very day.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.31,0:05:16.03,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Neil and... Pamela?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.54,0:05:37.43,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.07,0:05:39.96,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I wish I could pretend I hadn't seen them.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.75,0:05:46.69,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Given the circumstances of our engagement, \NI knew I couldn't expect love.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.88,0:05:53.50,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,But even so, I must face him with sincerity.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.20,0:05:57.09,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,We need to talk things out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.90,0:06:08.99,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,What a beautiful lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.01,0:06:14.07,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Um... My name is Constance Grail.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.55,0:06:16.60,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I hate to pry, but are you feeling all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.60,0:06:18.35,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What fun it looks.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.78,0:06:21.85,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Won't you come inside?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.22,0:06:24.60,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,May I?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.90,0:06:27.68,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What? But of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.12,0:06:34.87,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I'm in!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.23,0:06:38.88,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You have my gratitude, girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.88,0:06:41.01,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,"G-Girl"?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.20,0:06:50.33,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,What should I say to Neil?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.46,0:06:53.67,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.65,0:06:58.65,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,C-Congratulations on your engagement.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.56,0:07:01.44,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.71,0:07:04.52,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,If I remember correctly,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.07,0:07:07.34,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I often see her with Pamela.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.76,0:07:16.22,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Brenda, your hairpin is falling out.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.31,0:07:20.04,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Perhaps you should just take it off.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.04,0:07:23.20,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, I think I will.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.41,0:07:26.76,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,There. That's better.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.70,0:07:33.40,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,I left my purse on the second floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.40,0:07:38.68,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,Would you hold on to my hairpin for me\N while I go and fetch it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.68,0:07:42.10,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Yes, of course. Think nothing of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.95,0:07:57.34,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Brenda's been gone a long time...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.34,0:07:59.83,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Constance Grail!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.07,0:08:06.34,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,You've behaved outrageously.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.34,0:08:08.99,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Pamela? Neil?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.34,0:08:12.34,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,I know that your family is in dire straits,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.76,0:08:16.23,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,but don't you think \Nyou've taken this too far?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.52,0:08:19.67,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,To be frank, I question your character.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.67,0:08:21.97,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Wh-Whatever do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.97,0:08:24.58,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,My. You expect us to believe you ignorant?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.58,0:08:26.03,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,That simply won't do.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.03,0:08:30.48,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,I know that you stole Brenda's hairpin.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.28,0:08:37.76,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,I heard the whole story. \NNo sooner had you fixed her hair
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.76,0:08:41.13,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,than she realized her priceless pin was missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.38,0:08:47.37,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Tell me, Constance Grail, \Nwhat do you say to that?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.79,0:08:49.74,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.33,0:08:55.77,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,I'm sure someone in need of coin\Nwould have done anything for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.00,0:08:59.01,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Yes, I'm painfully aware of how you must feel.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.01,0:09:02.76,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,I know all about your family's \Nlamentable situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.67,0:09:06.76,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,B-But Brenda asked me to...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.76,0:09:09.64,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Then show us your purse.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.91,0:09:15.40,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,If you're no thief, \Nthat shouldn't pose a problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.70,0:09:21.16,Default,Neil,0,0,0,,Constance, you didn't...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.11,0:09:23.17,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.39,0:09:30.91,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Oh, dear me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.22,0:09:35.05,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,And what do we have here?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.05,0:09:37.42,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,I would implore you for an explanation.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.42,0:09:38.84,Default,Nobles,0,0,0,,So she did steal it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.84,0:09:40.31,Default,Nobles,0,0,0,,A Grail, of all people?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.46,0:09:43.60,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Brenda asked me to hold on to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.35,0:09:47.33,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,She asked you to hold on to this?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.33,0:09:50.14,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Even though you barely know each other?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.14,0:09:52.94,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,I find that hard to believe.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.44,0:09:55.63,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Brenda!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.57,0:09:58.07,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Please, tell them!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.07,0:10:00.20,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You asked me, remember?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.20,0:10:03.20,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You asked me to hold on to it\N while you got your purse!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.20,0:10:04.66,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You remember, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.61,0:10:08.95,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Why won't you tell them, Brenda?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.22,0:10:11.32,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Brenda, please!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.62,0:10:14.71,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Your excuses are growing disgraceful.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.60,0:10:20.62,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Look, poor Brenda is frightened.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.62,0:10:22.34,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,It's all right, Brenda.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.88,0:10:25.25,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,You needn't say a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.00,0:10:28.49,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,There you have it, Neil.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.49,0:10:30.98,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,You see what Constance is like.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.98,0:10:35.34,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,You ought to object \Nto your engagement at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.75,0:10:38.44,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,She's committed a crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.44,0:10:42.85,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,People will lose confidence in \Nthe Bronson Company if you marry her.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.85,0:10:46.23,Default,Neil,0,0,0,,But there's no proof that she stole it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.61,0:10:47.96,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Proof?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.24,0:10:53.76,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Why, everyone here is a witness!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.09,0:10:59.32,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,I know. Viscount Hamsworth \Nis a man of the cloth.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.32,0:11:02.76,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,You could lodge your objection with him now.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.76,0:11:05.34,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You're wrong! I would never steal!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.34,0:11:07.25,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,"Be you sincere"?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.11,0:11:10.64,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,So much for the Grail family's sincerity.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.64,0:11:13.27,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,You're nothing but a common thief.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.27,0:11:14.78,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You're wrong...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.99,0:11:31.53,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.55,0:11:38.59,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Someone, anyone, help me!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.34,0:11:40.77,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Help!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.53,0:11:42.95,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.58,0:11:48.39,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I'll help you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.28,0:11:51.70,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Who's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.84,0:11:55.16,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,But in exchange...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.63,0:12:06.07,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,A thief, you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.45,0:12:11.08,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I wonder...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.08,0:12:14.55,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Which of us is the real thief?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.42,0:12:21.51,Main - Italics,Pamela,0,0,0,,Constance Grail...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.18,0:12:26.28,Main - Italics,Pamela,0,0,0,,She makes such a show \Nof her ridiculous "sincerity."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.28,0:12:28.82,Main - Italics,Pamela,0,0,0,,I've never been able to stomach her.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.58,0:12:33.27,Main - Italics,Pamela,0,0,0,,Yet she gets engaged to {\i0}the{\i1} Neil Bronson?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.02,0:12:39.72,Main - Italics,Pamela,0,0,0,,Why should she get special treatment\Nwhen her looks and her family's wealth
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.72,0:12:42.28,Main - Italics,Pamela,0,0,0,,can't hold a candle to mine?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.64,0:12:47.81,Main - Italics,Pamela,0,0,0,,That's why I decided to use Brenda \Nto crush her! So how...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.52,0:12:51.92,Main - Top,Pamela,0,0,0,,Me, a thief? Whatever do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.92,0:12:53.84,Main - Top,Pamela,0,0,0,,I won't stand for such slanderous—
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.08,0:12:55.04,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Well, were you aware...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.44,0:13:02.29,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,that I am engaged to the man you were\Nso shamelessly rutting with in the shrubbery?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.43,0:13:07.79,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,I... I did no such thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.79,0:13:09.92,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Neil and I kissed, nothing more!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.92,0:13:11.17,Default,Neil,0,0,0,,Pamela!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.69,0:13:14.19,Default,Nobles,0,0,0,,They kissed?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.19,0:13:16.68,Default,Nobles,0,0,0,,The rumors are true, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.68,0:13:19.61,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh dear. It seems I misspoke.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.61,0:13:23.07,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You {\i1}were{\i0} only kissing...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.95,0:13:26.33,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,another woman's fiancé.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.70,0:13:30.20,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,But surely you can see the thievery.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.52,0:13:36.20,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,That still doesn't change the fact \Nthat you stole Brenda's hairpin!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.62,0:13:37.88,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.46,0:13:41.33,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Say, you there.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.58,0:13:45.02,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Give me a moment. Let me search my memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.55,0:13:47.59,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Ah, yes. Wayne.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.04,0:13:49.83,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Wayne Hastings.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.16,0:13:52.47,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You saw us, did you not?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.81,0:13:54.84,Default,Wayne,0,0,0,,I... I don't...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.84,0:13:58.34,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,If you'd rather not speak up, so be it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.34,0:14:00.32,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,But tread carefully.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.32,0:14:03.84,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Many others know the truth as well as you do.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.84,0:14:07.99,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,As it happens, I have an excellent memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.36,0:14:10.36,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Viscountess Stan,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.36,0:14:12.36,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Miss Bower,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.36,0:14:15.30,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,and Knight Pelham were all there.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.68,0:14:16.87,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Additionally...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.68,0:14:23.12,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,you there in the lemon dress, \Nalthough it seems she does not know your name.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.10,0:14:28.26,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,All four of you were looking at us\Nat the time, were you not?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.97,0:14:31.75,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Never mind, ladies and gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.12,0:14:35.29,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You don't have to say a word.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.29,0:14:39.14,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,However, as I detest awkward ambiguities,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.48,0:14:42.02,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I will ask you once more.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.45,0:14:46.52,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Wayne Hastings! Stop staring \Nat your shoes and look at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.88,0:14:50.77,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,That's better.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.77,0:14:53.98,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Now, Wayne, give me \Nthe benefit of your opinion.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.28,0:15:00.54,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Is it right to frame an innocent person\N for a crime they did not commit?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.93,0:15:05.66,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What of those who know the truth \Nbut choose to remain silent for their own sakes?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.47,0:15:09.17,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'll tell you what I think.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.42,0:15:12.42,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Anyone who does such a thing will go to hell,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.42,0:15:15.68,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,and those who turn a blind eye\N are equally guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.25,0:15:20.65,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Now, Wayne, I'd like you to imagine something.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.65,0:15:23.84,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Should the truth ever come to light,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.84,0:15:29.01,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,where would that leave you, \Nand what will people say about you?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.45,0:15:32.94,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Look at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.92,0:15:37.63,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I won't allow you to take your eyes off me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.01,0:15:40.93,Default,Wayne,0,0,0,,I... I saw.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.90,0:15:45.70,Default,Wayne,0,0,0,,I saw it. Miss Grail didn't steal anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.70,0:15:49.11,Default,Wayne,0,0,0,,All she did was neaten Brenda's hair.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.49,0:15:55.21,Default,Wayne,0,0,0,,And Brenda asked her to hold on to that hairpin!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.21,0:15:57.71,Default,Lemon Dress Lady,0,0,0,,I... I heard that as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.73,0:16:00.55,Default,Viscountess Stan,0,0,0,,I also saw them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.55,0:16:01.37,Default,Lady Blois,0,0,0,,As did I.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.37,0:16:02.97,Default,Pelham,0,0,0,,It happened just as she said!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.37,0:16:06.43,Default,Neil,0,0,0,,Is this true, Pamela?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.23,0:16:10.29,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Neil! N-No!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.29,0:16:11.85,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,I mean, Brenda—
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.14,0:16:13.34,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Oh, of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.31,0:16:16.36,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Brenda lied to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.64,0:16:21.12,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Look, poor Brenda is frightened.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.84,0:16:25.16,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,It's all right, Brenda.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.16,0:16:27.05,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You needn't say a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.94,0:16:34.89,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,My.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.34,0:16:38.13,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,What is all this fuss about?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.71,0:16:42.65,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, it's the nouveau riche hog. {\i1}Lovely.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.89,0:16:44.89,Default,Servant,0,0,0,,My lord, as it happens...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.15,0:16:47.64,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Ah, I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.92,0:16:50.79,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,You've had an unfortunate evening, Miss Grail.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.79,0:16:52.52,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Yes, dreadful.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.92,0:16:56.97,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I wish to turn to the goddesses \Nin the face of such mistreatment.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.97,0:16:59.03,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Might I trouble you to assist me?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.03,0:17:03.29,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,In objecting to your engagement, you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.56,0:17:05.76,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Will it be accepted?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.76,0:17:10.47,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Not at once, I fear, since your engagement \Nhas already been made public.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.47,0:17:13.88,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,The other party has a right to speak, \Nso an appropriate venue would—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.88,0:17:16.55,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,That is none of my concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.15,0:17:24.31,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Spare me your quibbles \Nand annul my engagement,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.31,0:17:26.06,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,you dithering fool.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.81,0:17:29.81,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Otherwise...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.81,0:17:36.36,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,the world will know that Dominic Hamsworth\N hosted a party tonight at the Grand Merillian
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.36,0:17:42.33,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,where couples conducted themselves \Nscandalously in the exalted royal gardens.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.33,0:17:47.83,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,And I will personally stop at nothing\N to ensure that His Royal Majesty hears of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.60,0:17:51.43,Main - Italics,Pamela,0,0,0,,Who is this woman?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.43,0:17:55.08,Main - Italics,Pamela,0,0,0,,She's nothing like the Constance Grail I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.14,0:18:02.61,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Ladies and gentlemen,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.20,0:18:08.60,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I sincerely apologize for casting \Na pall over this splendid occasion.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.22,0:18:13.78,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I hope you will bless this young couple \Nburning with illicit love.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.00,0:18:18.08,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Now, if you will all excuse me...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.37,0:18:24.62,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Please, wait a moment!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.17,0:18:35.20,Default,Countess Emanuel,0,0,0,,I gave my best wishes \Nto Miss Grail, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.20,0:18:39.89,Default,Countess Emanuel,0,0,0,,So I found your antics somewhat vexing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.30,0:18:43.88,Default,Countess Emanuel,0,0,0,,Did you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.19,0:18:48.89,Default,Countess Emanuel,0,0,0,,Where I come from, thieves are\N made to wear burning-hot shoes...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.20,0:18:52.66,Default,Countess Emanuel,0,0,0,,and dance until they die.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.30,0:18:59.65,Default,Count,0,0,0,,Ah, it's begun.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.65,0:19:01.16,Default,Count,0,0,0,,The first in ten years.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.16,0:19:04.74,Default,Lady,0,0,0,,I wonder how long those children will last.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.74,0:19:07.92,Default,Elderly Lady,0,0,0,,I must say, Constance gave me quite a shock.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.17,0:19:09.91,Default,Elderly Lady,0,0,0,,I could almost have believed...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.91,0:19:15.42,Default,Elderly Lady,0,0,0,,that Scarlett Castiel had returned from hell.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.88,0:19:24.21,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,A dream?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.92,0:19:26.38,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,It was just a dream!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.39,0:19:32.89,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You're awake at last, Constance Grail.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.39,0:19:40.36,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Wh-Wh-What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.36,0:19:44.40,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Whatever do you mean? \NAre you still half asleep?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.00,0:19:49.53,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Um... Whom do I have \Nthe pleasure of addressing?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.77,0:19:55.03,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I am Scarlett Castiel.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.50,0:20:02.91,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Wait, wait, wait. You must be joking.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.91,0:20:06.05,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Scarlett Castiel was executed ten years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.05,0:20:07.31,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Goodness, girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.19,0:20:09.55,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Tell me...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.03,0:20:13.00,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Do I look alive to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.40,0:20:16.94,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,B-But...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.99,0:20:21.58,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Scarlett Castiel was \Nthe wickedest woman of her age.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.16,0:20:26.33,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,She even plotted to poison \NMiss Cecilia, her rival in love.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.03,0:20:31.56,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Crown Prince Enrique unmasked her \Nat the Grand Merillian
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.56,0:20:33.82,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,and ended their engagement.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.09,0:20:38.43,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,But she'd behaved so monstrously \Nthat she was put to death as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.03,0:20:42.46,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,That's certainly {\i1}one{\i0} way to sum it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.04,0:20:47.46,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I don't remember a thing \Nabout the day of my execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.33,0:20:50.85,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,But the Grand Merillian, \Nwhere we met yesterday,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.32,0:20:56.61,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,is where that brainless Enrique \Nand scheming Cecilia humiliated me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.74,0:21:00.21,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Even now, just thinking of it is infuriating.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.99,0:21:04.74,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,H-How can you speak of the prince that way?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.74,0:21:07.24,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Or call the crown princess "scheming"?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.68,0:21:11.11,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,In any case, the next thing I knew, \NI found myself there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.11,0:21:14.12,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,But try as I might, I couldn't enter the hall.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.04,0:21:19.37,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,It must have been thanks to you\N that I finally managed it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.69,0:21:24.39,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You were the first person to ever notice me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.71,0:21:32.39,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You seem plain, dull, \Nand generally unremarkable,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.39,0:21:37.37,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,but you may take pride in the fact \Nthat you can see me, if nothing else!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.37,0:21:39.63,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,That feels a tad harsh.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.23,0:21:42.98,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Still, what are you doing in my house?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.98,0:21:46.15,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Why, because I have yet to receive my due.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.78,0:21:48.04,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your due?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.75,0:21:50.78,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,My, have you forgotten?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.78,0:21:54.40,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Surely you didn't think I would help \Na perfect stranger for nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.46,0:21:57.69,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.69,0:21:59.04,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I'll help you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.35,0:22:01.25,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,But in exchange...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.16,0:22:04.80,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Listen well, Constance Grail.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.84,0:22:12.77,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You will spend the rest of your life \Nensuring that I have my revenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.31,0:22:16.98,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your... revenge?
